- - - - - - - - - - regression tests - - - - - - - - - -

The following features are documented but lack automated test coverage.
Listed roughly in order of value vs. effort.

Medium priority:

- vhost.sh: two server{} blocks on different ports, each with its own
  webroot; verify the right content is served per port/hostname.

- useragent.sh: configure user-agent-deny with a pattern; verify
  matching UA gets 403, non-matching UA gets 200.

- custom-error.sh: place errors/404.html in webroot; request a missing
  file and verify the custom page content is returned.

- keepalive.sh: issue two GET requests over a single TCP connection;
  verify both succeed without the connection being closed in between.

- cache.sh: configure max-age; verify the response for a static file
  includes Cache-Control: max-age=N matching the configured value.

Lower priority (more setup required):

- throttle.sh: configure a very low byte rate for a URL pattern; time
  a transfer and verify it is rate-limited accordingly.

- ssl.sh: generate a self-signed cert; verify curl --insecure gets 200
  over HTTPS and that HTTP->HTTPS redirect works.  Also cover the
  startup cert validity check: expired/future certs refuse to start,
  -k overrides.

- symlink.sh: create a symlink pointing outside the webroot with
  check-symlinks = true; verify the request returns 403.

Skip / manual only:

- chroot.sh: requires root privileges; not suitable for CI.
- referer.sh: check-referer behaviour; finicky to test reliably.
- compression-level.sh: zlib level tuning; low regression risk.
- signal.sh: USR1/USR2 (log reopen / graceful restart); manual only.

- - - - - - - - - - later - - - - - - - - - -

Let command line options override port/host etc. that are in the global
section of the config file.  Today the config file wins over -p.

Extend the location directive with per-PATTERN settings, so max-age can
be set for parts of a site rather than for all files, which may
otherwise mess up reloading, e.g. a blog:

  location "PATTERN" {
       max-age = 2d
       add-header {
           key   = "Cache-Control"
           value = "public, no-transform"
       }
       gzip = true
  }

Look into compressing CGI and ls() output using fmemopen().

Make open in mmc.c use O_NONBLOCK flag, to prevent DOS attack via
a named pipe?

Document how symlinks interact with .htpasswd - authorization is checked
on the result of the symlink, and not the origin.

Change redirect to put the Refresh command in the HTTP headers, instead of
a META tag.

Add TCP_NODELAY, but after CGIs get spawned.

Add stat cache?  1 minute expiry?

Ifdef the un-close-on-exec CGI thing for Linux only.

- - - - - - - - - - someday - - - - - - - - - -

The special world-permissions checking is probably bogus.  For one
thing, it doesn't handle restrictive permissions on parent directories
properly.  It should probably just go away.

redirect should interpret a path with a trailing / as /index.html

ssi should change $cwd to the source document's location.

Allow .throttle files in individual directories.

Log-digesting scripts.

Config web page.
    Common errors:
	Not realizing that -c overrides CGI_PATTERN instead of augmenting it.
	Using a directory name for the -c pattern.

- - - - - - - - - - 3.x - - - - - - - - - -

Tasklets re-write.

Let server directives replace vhost matching.  When virtual-host=false
we can use either the title of the server directive or a separate
host/server-name setting for matching the incoming requests.
